WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.720
Stand on one leg.

2
00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:05.290
Your hip and your knee now
carry your whole weight.

3
00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:08.350
Lift the other foot and
draw a circle in the air.

4
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.320
The hip swings the whole leg with ease.

5
00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:14.580
Now keep your thigh still and
try it with the knee alone.

6
00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:15.830
No circle.

7
00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:19.280
So why can only one of them
swing your leg in a circle?

8
00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:22.000
In this mission, you'll
look inside a joint:

9
00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:27.640
smooth cartilage caps, a slippery fluid,
and tough bands holding it together.

10
00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:31.450
Then you'll untangle two
cords that are easy to mix up:

11
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:36.050
ligaments join bone to bone,
tendons join muscle to bone.

12
00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:40.000
Your mission: explain why your hip
can swing your leg in a circle,

13
00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:41.480
but your knee cannot.
